#!/bin/bash
{{ template "lib.sh" . }}
{{ template "pin.sh" (dict "chezmoi" .chezmoi "name" "kbd-light") }}
# Only a Mac with both a keyboard light and an ambient light sensor: the MacBook, not the mini.
if ! compgen -G '/sys/class/leds/*kbd_backlight' >/dev/null || ! compgen -G '/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device*/in_illuminance_input' >/dev/null || systemd-detect-virt -q --container; then
  log "kbd-light: no keyboard light and light sensor here"
  exit 0
fi
tarball=$(pin_fetch)
tar -xzf "$tarball" -C "$pin_tmp"
src=$pin_tmp/kbd-light-$pin_version
make -C "$src" >/dev/null || die "kbd-light: build failed"
# The unit runs /usr/bin/aurora-kbd-light, so the prefix stays /usr.
root make -C "$src" install PREFIX=/usr >/dev/null || die "kbd-light: install failed"
root systemctl daemon-reload
root systemctl enable aurora-kbd-light.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || die "kbd-light: could not enable its unit"
root systemctl restart aurora-kbd-light.service || die "kbd-light: its unit did not start"
pin_done
